==English==
{{was wotd|2009|March|29}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|alk.}}

===Etymology===
First attested in 1677. From {{m|en|alkali}}, ultimately from {{der|en|ar|قلي|اَلْقِلْي|alkali, ashes of the [[saltwort]]}}, related to {{m|ar|قَلَى||to roast in a pan, fry}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈæl.kəl.aɪn/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{enPR|ălˈkəlīn}}, {{IPA|/ˈæl.kə.laɪn/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-alkaline.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-au-alkaline.ogg|Audio (AU)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An [[alkaline battery]].

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Of, or relating to an [[alkali]], one of a class of caustic bases.
# {{lb|en|chemistry}} Having a [[pH]] greater than 7.

